1. What is Encapsulation?

Encapsulation is the process of combining data and methods into a single unit called a class and restricting direct access to data.

We commonly achieve encapsulation using:

private variables

public getter and setter methods

Example

class Student {
    private String name;
    private int age;

    public void setName(String name) {
        this.name = name;
    }

    public String getName() {
        return name;
    }

    public void setAge(int age) {
        if (age > 0) {
            this.age = age;
        }
    }

    public int getAge() {
        return age;
    }
}

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Student s = new Student();

        s.setName("Manjula");
        s.setAge(21);

        System.out.println(s.getName());
        System.out.println(s.getAge());
    }
}

Output

Manjula
21
